  "notes": "ADR-045 contract wire complete — 3 Decision items all implemented.\n\n## IP1 — collectResults inline status mutation\nAdded exported `applyStatusMutation(taskRef, result)` helper at top of result-collector.ts (lines 80–100) implementing ADR-045 Decision 1 mapping: DONE→TaskStatus.DONE, GO_WITH_TECH_DEBT→TaskStatus.DONE (debt-DONE, ADR-045 Consequences), NO_GO→TaskStatus.NO_GO. Inside waitForResults, helper `syncTaskStatusFromResult` invokes applyStatusMutation after every result push: real .result (line 257), late EXIT-trap result (line 273), synthetic timeout NO_GO (line 296), final sweep (line 365). taskMap.get(taskId) returns the same in-memory reference held by sprint.tasks (Map<string, Task> referencing the array entries), so mutation propagates without disk write — Auditor git diff --stat boundary unaffected (ADR-037 safe).\n\n## IP2 — waitForResults main loop dep-aware respawn\nAdded `config?: ResolvedConfig` parameter to waitForResults signature (result-collector.ts line 197). Helper `maybeRespawn` (lines 326–334) guards on config?.dependency_pipeline_enabled; when true it dynamically imports respawnEligibleTasks (lazy import via `loadRespawn` cached, ADR-045 cycle avoidance) and invokes it with (projectRoot, sprint, config, spawnOpts). Two call-sites: (a) after initial collectResults+processQueue (line 348, race-safe Wave 2 immediate eligibility), (b) inside the while-loop after each newlyCollected+processQueue cycle (line 372). When config is omitted or flag is false, branch short-circuits — legacy FIFO behavior preserved bit-exact (Sprint 164 default safety).\n\n## IP3 — Caller signature pass-through\n- sprint-controller.ts::waitForResults wrapper now accepts `config?: ResolvedConfig` (line 221) and forwards to waitForResultsImpl (line 229).\n- sprint-controller.ts runSprint EXECUTE phase call (line 486) now passes `config`.\n- sprint-phases.ts runFixPhase call (line 1038) now passes `config`.\nAll parameters optional → no breaking change for tests or external callers.\n\n## IP4 — Lazy import cycle break\nsprint-spawner.ts already imports resolveAgentPrompt/resolveSkillPrompts from result-collector.ts, so a counter-import would create a module-init cycle. Solution: `import type { respawnEligibleTasks as RespawnFn }` (type-only, no runtime cost) + `let cachedRespawn` + `async function loadRespawn()` that performs `await import('./sprint-spawner.js')` on first invocation and caches the function reference. This defers the actual dependency resolution to runtime (after both modules have fully loaded) and preserves the type contract.\n\n## Test — tests/orchestra/dependency-pipeline-wire.test.ts\n9 tests (8 directives + 1 additional NO_GO mutation assertion), all PASS:\n- (a) enabled:false → respawnEligibleTasks returns [], status preserved, no worker spawn\n- (b) Wave 1 (3 DONE tasks) → Wave 2 (deps on all 3) spawned, status EXECUTING\n- (c) Chained 3-wave: Wave 3 spawn when Wave 1+2 both DONE (Kahn topological coverage)\n- (d) NO_GO Wave 1 → Wave 2 dep stays PENDING (filter rejects non-DONE)\n- (e) Slot saturation: maxWorkers=2, 3 eligible → first 2 spawn (resolveEffectiveWorkers mock)\n- (f) GO_WITH_TECH_DEBT applied via applyStatusMutation → TaskStatus.DONE → Wave 2 spawn (ADR-045 Consequences)\n- (g) Inline mutation timing: before mutation Wave 2 ineligible; after mutation Wave 2 spawned (atomic same-tick proof) + extra NO_GO mutation assertion\n- (h) currentlyExecuting === maxWorkers → slotsAvailable=0 → idempotent no-spawn\n\n## Verification (all PASS)\n- `grep -nE \"respawnEligibleTasks\" src/orchestra/result-collector.ts` → 7 matches (req ≥2) ✓\n- `grep -nE \"taskRef.status = TaskStatus\" src/orchestra/result-collector.ts` → 3 matches (req ≥3) ✓\n- `grep -rn \"respawnEligibleTasks\" src/` → 15 matches across 3 files (req ≥4) ✓\n- `tsc --noEmit` → PASS (0 errors) ✓\n- `npx vitest run tests/orchestra/dependency-pipeline-wire.test.ts` → 9/9 PASS ✓\n- Regression sweep: dependency-pipeline.test.ts (20 tests, 2 skipped) + dependency-scheduler.test.ts (54) + cascade-unblock-wire.test.ts (5) + sprint-spawner.test.ts (59) + result-collector.test.ts (21) + result-evaluator.test.ts (131+9 typed) → 297 PASS ✓\n- Sprint 159 survivor: evaluate-phase-idempotency.test.ts → 6/6 PASS ✓ (status mutation timing change does not break idempotency)\n\n## Pre-existing failures (NOT caused by this task)\nFull suite ran with 17 failures (16,230 PASS, 66 skipped). All 17 failures verified identical via git-stash baseline diff — they pre-exist:\n- fix-phase-map.test.ts (5) — Sprint 159 chronic regression that Task 2 of Sprint 164 targets\n- sprint-phases-rollback.test.ts (3), brain-provider.test.ts (2), docker-backend.test.ts (2), gemini-integration.test.ts (2), github-pages-deploy.test.ts (1), ci-workflow.test.ts (1), workflows/ci.test.ts (1)\nZero new regressions introduced.\n\n## Config freeze respected\nNo change to .deckent/config.json — `dependency_pipeline_enabled` remains at its default (Sprint 164 anchor rule). Wire is dormant in legacy FIFO mode until Sprint 165 flip.",
